    faqs:
      - { q: "A church that's very much alive", a: ["Lifepoint is a growing and vibrant church in Moreton Bay. Whoever said that the church is dying forgot to tell these people. It is a place and people known in this region for being incredibly welcoming and strangely authentic, people just seem real (even if they are messy)."] }
      - { q: "It's all about Jesus", a: ["We always talk about Jesus, and we believe he is the way, the truth and the life. We believe he was who he claimed to be, and that through him everyone is being called into God's family. We believe that God is calling you to be forgiven, redeemed and sent!"] }
      - { q: Something real is happening here, a: ["There is a tangible and undeniable sense of God being alive at Lifepoint. We love to pray and sing, experience God's presence and love and serve one another."] }
      - { q: Bible people in a modern world, a: ["We believe that the Bible is true and helpful. We love the Bible, preach the Bible, read the Bible, and most importantly, live by its often counter-cultural teaching."] }
      - { q: More than Sundays, a: ["We don't talk much about rules and religion at Lifepoint, we talk about love, grace, truth, and a strange new free and joyful way to live that involves a supernatural power called the Holy Spirit."] }
      - { q: A church of groups, a: ["Lifepoint is a church of groups. We have dozens of small groups and we take the home as seriously as we do our larger gatherings."] }
      - { q: Friendship at the heart, a: ["In a world where people have fewer people who really know them, Lifepoint is full of friendship. It is refreshing to see people who genuinely love each other, even though they all don't agree about everything and come from different social, cultural and religious backgrounds."] }
      - { q: A church for the next generation, a: ["There are so many young people here! We have hundreds of kids, teenagers and young adults at Lifepoint. Who would have thought it but these young people LOVE church, and are being trained as people who will make a difference in this world for good."] }
      - { q: A church of generosity and service, a: ["Lifepoint people get together in groups all the time and serve our needy, our disabled, our schools, the struggling, and offer real help in financial and other ways. It is a place people call upon because they know their mess will be met not with judgement, but grace and love."] }
      - { q: A church that equips and sends leaders, a: ["It is a training church, with the main focus being on loving God and loving others where people are already working and living. There are a very high number of leaders here."] }
